<!--
  NOT WIRED IN — see docs/PACKAGING.md, "Windows installer branding", and
  package-windows.ps1 (the --resource-dir block is commented out there).

  jpackage's --resource-dir mechanism is supposed to look up this exact
  filename ("overrides.wxi") to override WiX variables in its generated WiX
  project (documented at
  https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/jpackage/override-jpackage-resources.html
  as "WiX source file with WiX variables overrides"). Tried on a real
  Windows build with --resource-dir pointed at this directory: candle.exe
  itself failed to compile jpackage's generated main.wxs (exit code 104),
  and jpackage did not surface WiX's actual CNDL error text — so whatever is
  wrong (this file isn't being <?include?>'d where expected, a required
  search path is missing, the WixVariable syntax itself is wrong for this
  jpackage/WiX version, something else) is not yet known. Re-run with
  jpackage's own --verbose flag to get WiX's real error before touching this
  again.

  Intent, if it's ever made to work: WixUIBannerBmp is the 493x58 strip shown
  atop every wizard page except Welcome/Finish; WixUIDialogBmp is the
  493x312 full background of the Welcome/Finish pages. banner.bmp/dialog.bmp
  sit next to this file so the relative paths below would resolve
  regardless of the working directory candle.exe is invoked from — assuming
  that relative-path resolution is even correct, which was never confirmed.
-->
<WixVariable Id="WixUIBannerBmp" Value="banner.bmp" />
<WixVariable Id="WixUIDialogBmp" Value="dialog.bmp" />
